\subsection{Filtering}{

The \code{filter} argument can be supplied as either:
\itemize{
\item a named list of filters, interpreted as one filter set using AND logic; or
\item a list of named filter lists, interpreted using OR logic across filter sets
and AND logic within each filter set.
}

In a single named filter list, different columns are combined using AND logic.
For example:

\verb{#' list(taxon = "Exemplomygale currycomboides", feature = "male palp") #'}

matches figure records where \code{taxon} is \code{"Exemplomygale currycomboides"} and
\code{feature} is \code{"male palp"}.

Multiple accepted values can be supplied for one column. Values within the
same column are interpreted using OR logic. For example:

\verb{#' list(feature = c("male palp", "spermathecae")) #'}

matches figure records where \code{feature} is either \code{"male palp"} or
\code{"spermathecae"}.

These can be combined. For example:

\verb{#' list( #'   taxon = "Exemplomygale currycomboides", #'   feature = c("male palp", "spermathecae") #' ) #'}

matches figure records where \code{taxon} is \code{"Exemplomygale currycomboides"} and
\code{feature} is either \code{"male palp"} or \code{"spermathecae"}.

A list of named filter lists can be used to express alternative filter sets.
The alternative sets are combined using OR logic, while conditions within each
set are combined using AND logic. For example:

\verb{#' list( #'   list(sex = "male", feature = "male palp"), #'   list(sex = "female", feature = "spermathecae") #' ) #'}

matches figure records where \verb{(sex == "male" AND feature == "male palp")} OR
\verb{(sex == "female" AND feature == "spermathecae")}.

Filter columns may be ordinary character columns or list-columns. This allows
the function to work with metadata imported by \code{\link[=read_taxRmatic_figures]{read_taxRmatic_figures()}},
including automatically split \code{specimen_code} values and user-selected
multi-value metadata columns.
