\subsection{Figure-reference styles}{

If \code{figure_reference_style = "full"}, each selected figure record is listed
individually, for example \code{"1A, 1B, 1C"}.

If \code{figure_reference_style = "compact"}, consecutive figure numbers or
figure parts are collapsed into ranges where possible, for example
\code{"1A–C"}.

If all labelled parts of a figure are selected, the part labels are dropped
and the whole figure is cited instead. For example, if all parts of Figure 1
are selected, the reference is simplified to \code{"Fig. 1"} rather than listing
every part.
}
