This function formats references for figures that match the metadata or filter you supply, for example \verb{Fig. 2A–C}. Most users will not need to call it directly: description, diagnosis and compilation functions use it internally when they add figure references.

If a reference is missing or too broad, check the figure table and filter rather than typing the figure number into the description. See \code{parse_figure_filter()} and the vignette on preparing CSV data.
